<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nibelungenlied</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1200</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nibelungenlied is a Middle High German epic poem written around 1200, probably in the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passau">Passau</a>. It tells of the hero Siegfried, his murder at the Burgundian court of Worms, and the revenge of his widow Kriemhild, which ends in the destruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> at the court of the Hunnic king Etzel. The story draws on memories of the Burgundian kingdom destroyed in 436.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nibelungenlied.jpg" alt="Nibelungenlied" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nibelungenlied_manuscript-c_f1r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
